    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini-hiPatterns\n\n### Description\n\nI'm really enjoying `mini-hiPatterns`. Thanks! 💯 \r\n\r\nHere are some examples that would be great for the readme and/or the docs:\r\n\r\n- highlight entire line, but only when line starts with a particular string\r\n- highlight entire line, but only when line ends with a particular string\r\n- highlight entire line when line, but only when:\r\n  - line starts with a particular string, or\r\n  - line end with a particular string, or\r\n  - line contains a particular string, with whitespace on either side (like the existing example in the docs)\r\n\r\nAlso, this is not on `mini.nvim` at all, but if it was possible, it would be amazing if there were also links to:\r\n- a definitive guide to using Lua's frontier patterns\r\n- a snippet that shows how to read all existing styles on a highlight group so they can be incorporated into the call to `vim.api.nvim_set_hl()`",
